From e89e20e18772821dd527ffddd03d98fe04ba3158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:06:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] refactor(art): rewrite to the CDN unconditionally and
 let its 404 pick the rung
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces "measure which printings have localized art, then choose one" with the
mechanism the standalone phase-rs-zh bookmarklet already proved out: rewrite EVERY
Scryfall image URL to the community CDN, and let that CDN's own 404 fall to its
English mirror.

The old design could not be made consistent. Choosing a printing means asking
"which printings does this locale have?" up front, and the answer was a ~1.6 MB
generated table consulted independently by every entry point at its own moment —
so two entry points could answer differently for the same card and the same frame.
Observed: Seasoned Pyromancer rendered as `2x2 #454` (Chinese) in hand and
`2x2 #123` (English) on the stack.

The new design has nothing to disagree about. A card's localized image is the SAME
printing id on another host, so the rewrite keeps whatever printing it was handed;
the CDN answers 404 for printings it has no art for, and the existing rung ladder
(`derivedArtSource` already returned `{url, fallback}`) drops to that host's
English image. Same printing in every zone by construction.

Deleted with it: the availability table, its loader, the canonical-printing cache
added earlier in this session, and the printing-selection helpers. Measured over
the pool, 35% of printings resolve from the CDN directly and 65% take the 404
rung — and the `sf` rung covers all of those (8/8 sampled), so the ladder needs no
third tier.

`art_crop` now rewrites too, to the language-neutral prefix: the crop is the
illustration alone, and the CDN serves no localized crop at all, so sending it to
the localized prefix would spend a guaranteed 404 on every hover preview.
